# Swasthya Setu — environment template.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; keep it that way.
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the app still runs and
# every flow still completes, because both AI paths degrade to a deterministic
# local result rather than to an error.


# ─── Server-side only. Never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, never sent to the client. ───
#
# Google AI Studio key for gemini-2.5-flash, read exclusively by the route
# handlers under app/api/. Unset means no network inference is attempted at all:
# triage falls back to the keyword classifier and the longitudinal summary is
# composed from a local template, both visibly labelled as such.
#
# This key is deliberately absent from the Android build. See lib/api-base.ts.
GEMINI_API_KEY=


# ─── Client-side. Inlined into the bundle at build time. Origins only. ───
#
# Absolute origin of the deployment that serves app/api/, e.g.
# https://swasthya-setu.vercel.app  — no trailing slash.
#
# Leave EMPTY for web development and for the hosted deployment itself: an empty
# value means same-origin, which is what a bare /api/... already resolves to.
#
# Set it ONLY for the Android APK, where the document loads from file:// and a
# same-origin /api/... resolves to nothing. In CI this comes from the repository
# variable `API_BASE_URL`; see .github/workflows/android.yml.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=


# ─── Build-time only. Selects what `next build` emits. ───
#
# Set to `apk` to make next.config.ts turn on `output: 'export'` and emit a
# static out/ bundle for Capacitor. Leave UNSET everywhere else — including on
# the hosted deployment — to get a normal server build, which is the only kind
# that can actually run the route handlers under app/api/.
#
# You almost certainly do not want this in .env.local: setting it locally makes
# `npm run build` stop producing the API routes. CI sets it on one step only; see
# .github/workflows/android.yml.
BUILD_TARGET=
